00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:46.070
Actually, we have a real
cucumber farmer in Japan

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:49.030
who used these same technologies
to build his own cucumber

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:49.940
sorter.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:53.340
And he spent only $15 to
build his own cucumber

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:57.230
sorter by using Google Cloud
machine learning technology.

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.820
TIMOTHY JORDAN:
That's really cool,

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.195
DREA ALPHONSO: So
essentially, it

00:17:00.195 --> 00:17:03.386
takes the best prototype of
that, and kind of buckets them?

00:17:03.386 --> 00:17:04.010
KAZ SATO: Yeah.

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:09.950
So he wanted to build a machine
that can sort out all cucumbers

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.720
into nine different classes.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.579
And he took a [INAUDIBLE]
different models

00:17:13.579 --> 00:17:15.170
for his cucumbers.

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:18.410
And also build the sorter
by using the Raspberry Pi

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.500
and download the TensorFlow,
the machine learning library

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.450
from Google to build
his own sorter.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.010
And the point here
is that you don't

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:28.357
